Z||000036||fierohoho||07-23-2001||05:50 PM||||Hey, no hard feelings. It's all in fun.<P>Welcome to the forum.<P>Let's all remember that anything you do to your car, whether it's for looks or performance makes you a "Hot Rodder".<P>That puts us all into the same catagory just different sections for the cars we like.<P>To quote a Californian,"Can't we all just get along". <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000037||JDOGG1||07-23-2001||07:16 PM||||I just wanted to let the people who are still dissing me know that I didn't come on here in the first place and start my own log on name just to give people crap. I read a message that was left on our clubs guestbook telling me to check out this page and see what he said about our cars (Tweek).I never was the "True Player" you guys seem to think I want to be...I still listen to Metallica!!!<BR>I like rap but thats about it,its all wigger crap and I'm not like that.I want to say that whoever didn't read the original message will never know what they are talking about.This has all been settled and the guys are actually pretty cool.Lets just appreciate the fact that some of us want to keep the "Sport compact" look alive.Its our thing,I apoligized,and if you don't understand..talk to other people on this site,they are cool with me now,they just don't like my attempt at a so called "pimped out ride".At lest it doesn't say something like "TYPE R" on it!!!||||reg||10
Z||000038||Songman||07-23-2001||07:55 PM||||He did send me a message explaining why he posted this thread originally. I told him that although he had a motive, his methods may not have been the best possible approach. Instead of going through it all I will post my response to him and say that he seems alright. I suggested an apology to the people he insulted and it seems he has done that.<P>So I say to him.. Welcome to the forum...<P>Below is the message I sent him...<BR>---<BR>I don't have a problem with your motive. But you must admit that to come to an established group and start naming names and insulting people just because they disagree with you is going to cause more people to dislike you. I wouldn't have had a thing against you had it not been for that.<P>I have driven my hot rods throughtout the days of yup-mobiles and didn't mind that people in their BMW's looked down on my GTOs. That was their problem. I knew I had Porsches and Jaguars back home and drove what I drove by choice instead of necessity. And I dang sure wasn't trying to be accepted into any group just because of a car I drove. But, I also didn't go to a BMW board and start insulting people....<P>I feel the same way about your cars and your car club. If you like what you drive, who cares what anyone else thinks. I am sure a lot of people look at me funny when I drive one of my Fieros. That is their right. I know I have other cars at home to choose from but I enjoy my Fieros.<P>I have been a member of the Fiero board for a long time and for the most part we are all very friendly people. Sure, we have our problems even amongst ourselves at times, but when the smoke clears, we are still all friends. I'm willing to feel the same about you. One of the things that I am known for on the board is giving people the right to express themselves as long as they don't step on others by doing it. Sure, I am a pain in the ass sometimes about it but it is just who I am.<P>I say, forget this one incident. Make a brief apology to the people that you picked out to insult and then let it go. Feel free to be a member of the board. If you don't feel you want to do that, then I say instead of carrying it on it is best just to forget all about it. We have very few members in Maine and even those will probably never be consequential to your club. I think the direction this goes is up to you. Choose wisely... heheh.. No hard feelings on my part... I am sure I am a good bit older and more experienced than you are. If I can offer you a little advice it would be not to take so much to heart. Choose your battles and make sure it is something worth fighting for. Good luck to you.<P>Dale<P>Just so you'll know, I'm going to post this to the Fiero board with a little defense of your position. As I said above, it is your choice where it goes from here...<BR>---<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000039||Tonker||07-23-2001||08:00 PM||||At the risk of prolonging this thread, I'm going to insert my two cents (1.5 cents US).<BR><BR>I don't care for the car. Then again I don't care for Lamborghinis(sp?) either, so what the Hell do I know? I have a Geo Metro in addition to my Fiero, so I certainly can't criticise his ride.. Well I suppose I could but what's it going to serve? He probably doesn't understand our love for Fieros either. This our chance to convert another unsuspecting victim to our growing army of the undead!!!.. Uh wait, no.. that's not it at all...<BR><BR>JDogg is obviously proud is his car and rightfully so; he's put some work into it. I wouldn't choose to do what he's done, but I can appreciate his effort. I don't think his first post was particularly flattering either, but he was (I think) understandably upset and has since posted in a much more appropriate (and legible   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">) fashion. <BR><BR>So my suggestion is thus: rather than criticising his rice-mobile and "aural-death sound system" (not quoting anyone here, BTW) it would be more constructive to suggest the relative merits of competing systems vs his setup, if you choose to discuss it at all. From what I've seen this forum is for sharing knowledge and interests... and darn good at it I might add. Just look how smart I've become already!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Well look at me!!! Okay never mind   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR><BR>Anyway JDogg welcome to the forum, we'll have you sorted out and sitting behind the wheel of a Fiero in no time.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>---<BR>Edited for spelling and grammar *grr*.. stupid fingers; be less fat!!<BR><BR>------------------<BR>Black '86 Fiero GT.<BR>ICQ: 7813479<p>[This message has been edited by Tonker (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||3
