Z||000108||Oreif||08-22-2001||02:44 PM||||Ok Fierokiller, I'll race your little Fiat,<BR>You pick the time I'll pick the place.<BR>We can even have it filmed and posted on the net. <BR>The place I pick is Blackhawk Farms Race Course in Wisconsin. The fastest of 3 laps wins. I'll even let you run a few practice laps.<P>Why don't you just go to:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiatspider.com/1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiatspider.com/1.htm</A> <P>and flame away over there. <P>I think it is funny how these "people" always think there car is so much better than a Fiero that they need to come onto our forum and brag. What is the deal? Is a 13 to 18 year old Fiero suddenly the "standard" by which other cars are judged? Why is it when challenged on an actual race track they all chicken out? Even many morons around my town chicken out at the mention of going to a real race track.<P>Personally I think it's jealousy. They can't get there car to look good, go fast or handle as well as a Fiero for the low cost that we can.||||reg||2
Z||000109||Fierokiller||08-22-2001||08:29 PM||||hahahaha... I had my fun. But any way what do you guys have against the EK crew??<P>You make fun of there cars because they have a mystique in the club. They aren't a race club and they don't say they have fast cars.<P>Why take it to a race track. Your car can only perform on a race track?? I personally only take my car to the drag strip to run down the track between heats to see what it can do. I do most of my racing at the stop light. I think I type above my car will do 170 mph. That was a typo it only does 150 mph. <P>Most X 1/9 owners hate fiero's because they have the same body style as there older Fiat.<BR>But actually I was gonna buy a fiero but the fiat just fell into my lap. $200 for a car with a straight body and no rust and $50 more to get it on the road you can't blame me. It also doesn't take much money to make the fiat faster. Just longer to get parts.<P>Well I'm outta here. Just felt like sturring **** .<P>Hope u guys had fun with my post =)<P>Cya||||reg||1
Z||000110||Galen||08-22-2001||09:26 PM||||hehe..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> hehe.. I love using that little things  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> hehe, so ya say the fiero looks like a Fiat eh? yeah, well, ok. But ya know, let me think here for a second..... anyways.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You say you like going to a dragstrip? I'll say it and get flamed for it.. it takes alot less talent to drive a car in a straight line than it does to drive on a 'real race track' Yeah I like going fast in a straight line, right before I brake coming into a corner.. then I go fast in a straight line again after I'm out of the corner.. Bet that 'No Go' can't do that<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/sig.gif">  Ray -    <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>www.FieroLinks.f2s.com</A><BR>AIM: GalenRPG - ICQ: 98668558||||reg||1
Z||000111||Oreif||08-22-2001||09:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierokiller:<BR><B><P>Why take it to a race track. Your car can only perform on a race track?? I personally only take my car to the drag strip to run down the track between heats to see what it can do. I do most of my racing at the stop light. I think I type above my car will do 170 mph. That was a typo it only does 150 mph. <BR>But actually I was gonna buy a fiero but the fiat just fell into my lap. $200 for a car with a straight body and no rust and $50 more to get it on the road you can't blame me. It also doesn't take much money to make the fiat faster. Just longer to get parts.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My car can perform on the street. Aside from street racing being illegal, a track is better. It's more fun to race around on a road course and utilize the full potential of the car.<P>Besides you put up the challenge, I accepted, You declined once you found out it was on a race track.<P>(Basically, Put up or shut up)<P>As for your car being able to go 150mph, I doubt it. You must mean 150kmh. Even the Fiat forum listed above shows a 2.4 highly modded only gets to 140-150hp. His mods include 34adf carb, 9.8:1 pistons, cam upgrade, large valve head, and performance exhaust. The guy on there has track slips that show 1/4 mile times of 15.3 seconds and states that top speed on a highway of 125mph. That's close to what a STOCK V-6/5-spd Fiero gets! (15.4/128mph) With simular mods to a Fiero V-6 we're closer to 200hp and into the mid-14's. <P>See Ya (in my rear view mirror)<BR>||||reg||1
