Z||000113||Fierokiller||08-23-2001||01:35 AM||||Let me see I didn't recline a race. But Be realistic I'm not gonna drive my car to Wisconsin to prove I can beat you. My Fiat will do 150 mph. Whether some forum says a highly modded car will only do 140-150. I'm telling you what the board said when I was done with the run.<P>Cool... To bad I moved out of maine and thats no longer my e-mail. <P>and as far as your stock v6 in your fiero. hahaha... I have a fiat v6 that was going to go into the x1/9 but was instead used in the ferrari 206 & 246 Dino. When I get the time to rebuild that and modify it and my car to make it fit. I'll be looking at the big 200 mph. But until then I don't think I'll get higher than 150.<P>So suck a nut butt ****er ||||reg||1
Z||000114||Oreif||08-23-2001||01:56 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fierokiller:<BR><B>Let me see I didn't recline a race. But Be realistic I'm not gonna drive my car to Wisconsin to prove I can beat you. My Fiat will do 150 mph. Whether some forum says a highly modded car will only do 140-150. I'm telling you what the board said when I was done with the run.<P>Cool... To bad I moved out of maine and thats no longer my e-mail. <P>and as far as your stock v6 in your fiero. hahaha... I have a fiat v6 that was going to go into the x1/9 but was instead used in the ferrari 206 & 246 Dino. When I get the time to rebuild that and modify it and my car to make it fit. I'll be looking at the big 200 mph. But until then I don't think I'll get higher than 150.<P>So suck a nut butt ****er </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First, Re-read my post, It's 140 - 150 HORSEPOWER The top speed was 125MPH.<P>Second, As you say "That's what the board said", Does that mean at the end of the 1/4 mile!?!<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> <P>To get to 150 at the end of a 1/4 mile you need to be running 7-8 seconds. Hell most "super Stock" drag cars are 10 seconds at 125mph in the 1/4 mile.<P>As for swapping engines, We have a guy here with a 350 V-8 in his Fiero that's pushing OVER 400 HP! He drives it every weekend. Nothing needed to be modified to "make it fit" and it'll leave your imaginary Dino powered Fiat in the dust.<P>BTW ~ if your listed Email isn't any good, How did you get the password during registration?   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-23-2001).]||||reg||1
