Z||000116||Cheever3000||08-23-2001||02:51 AM||||(okay, you guys are keeping it going, so I got a penny's worth of opinion too)<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Why take it to a race track. Your car can only perform on a race track?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>No, the point is that <I>you</I> would have <B>no excuses</B> at a track!  None of that "Oh I wasn't ready" or "Had to slow for traffic" or "Dog ran into the street", etc etc etc.  It's always something with you freaks, and a track is put up or shut up.  And you come <I>ready</I>, or go home with nothing.<P>That's it from me on this topic.  I don't waste my time with ignoramuses like that.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000117||FieroKyle||08-23-2001||03:45 AM||||The funny thing is, for an anti Fiero guy who keep saying he is gonna leave cuz he don't like us, he always trys to come back with a wity statement. First his car does 180 mph, then 170, then 150, now 125. In a week his car will be running 85 mph and doing 1/4's in 30 seconds. Atleast we are getting to the bottom of this and the truth is starting to come around. Anyone in this forum with a the 2.8L V-6 would take this clown car Fiat anyday. They are fun to drive, but when you compare performance, we got ya there stock. Since you keep coming back to check this post, admit you are wrong, say your goodbyes, and never come back or unless two of the following happens. You post here in a friendly matter, not here to bash Fieros, or you own a Fiero. And everyone is happy.<P>Whoa, I feel like Stuart Smally saves the world! LMAO  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
