Z||000120||Voytek||08-23-2001||02:40 PM||||Man, just when I thought this thread had gone away it misteriously reappears, brought back to life by someone with no life.<P>May I suggest that next time you want to talk Fiats vs. Fieros go start a friendly new thread.<P>That said, read FieroKyle's post correctly.  He said that any STOCK 2.8 will take your Fiat.  STOCK = UNMODIFIED.<P>I've seen some nice Fiat X19's before and, I'm sure that many Fiero owners, including myself, feel some kind of sympathy towards the Fiat.  YOU are not helping here.<P>No matter what you say, here are some facts:<BR>- any stock Fiero GT will beat any stock Fiat X19 - slalom or drag.<BR>- Fieros don't rust - most Fiat X19's are   off the road today because they became rust buckets - read any automotive review and you'll see that this was a big problem.<BR>- While the Fiat looks kinda neat, it is a tiny box with below average safety, while the Fiero was only second to Volvo DL when it came out.<P>Need I go on?  I won't ever bash Fiats because they've made some awesome cars over the years but you should really give your head a shake dude!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000121||Fierokiller||08-23-2001||11:52 PM||||These are the specs I dug up on the x 1/9<P>1500 110mph (178kph) 11 sec 0-60mph<P>Now thats a stock car witht the stock 1.5. My car has a 2.4 and is modified considerably. So your telling me it's impossible to get that extra 40 mph?? <BR>The 2.4 gives me 20 mph faster than the 1.5.<BR>I've also added a better air intake, exhaust manifold, muffler, and have dont some machining on the cylinder head.<P>You might think I lie but I've put a lot of time in the car and a lot of different mechanics heads together. To get the power that I have gotten out of my car. <P>I race at the Medford track which is a mile long. The racers that go there for competition race the standard 1/4 mile but your can run up to 3/4 mile if you want.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000122||FieroKyle||08-24-2001||12:04 AM||||Even with your mods and different engine, yor Fiat still can't take a stock Fiero 2.8L. Although its not fast, its fast for a Fiat. We have an MG midget, thats race prepped and everything. Its faster than the MGB which is considerably faster than the Midgets. The midgets top out at 60 mph while the MGBs do a 100 mph. Our Midget can do about 110 mph, but it takes for ever, but 0-60 is great. however with this being a fast MG, it is not a fast car over all doing 0-60 in about 9 to 10 seconds. I know I am saying MGs to Fiats to Fieros, but I am just using my MG as an example to your Fiat. Yes, I am sure its a great car, but far as performance a Fiero has you beat even with your mods. So while I am sure you can beat almost any Fiat that is like yours, you can not however beat our Fieros.||||reg||1
